course: dictionary
lesson: 13430
title: Homogeneous: the same all the way through
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Homogeneous is a long word, but you can find its meaning with clues. Homo- often means same, and the rest tells you about kind. Together it means made of parts that are all alike. «The cake batter was homogeneous, with no lumps at all.» No lumps means every bit is the same, so homogeneous fits.
explain: Use the context to check. «Every player in the team wore a red shirt, so the team was homogeneous.» The red shirts show that everyone is alike, so a homogeneous group is one where all the members are of the same kind. Ask yourself: are all the parts the same? If yes, the word is probably homogeneous.
explain: Scientists use the word too. Salt fully dissolved in water looks the same everywhere, so it is a homogeneous mixture. Sand stirred into water is different: you can see the grains, so the mixture is heterogeneous, the opposite of homogeneous.
fact: Homogeneous means the same all the way through, with every part alike.
fact: A homogeneous group is made of people or things that are all of the same kind.
fact: «The paint was homogeneous» means every bit of the paint has the same colour and thickness.
fact: Salt fully dissolved in water is a homogeneous mixture, because it looks the same everywhere.
fact: The opposite of homogeneous is heterogeneous, which means made of parts that are different from each other.
exercise: «The cake batter was homogeneous, with no lumps at all.» What does homogeneous mean here? | Heavy to lift | Full of lumps and bits | Very hot from the oven | * Every part is the same
exercise: «Every player in the team wore a red shirt, so the team was homogeneous.» What does homogeneous mean in this sentence? | Very tall | Mixed up from many places | Only one player was there | * All of the same kind
exercise: Which of these is a homogeneous mixture? | A bag of mixed sweets | Sand stirred into water | * Salt fully dissolved in water | Pebbles mixed into a jar of rice
test: «The orange juice was homogeneous after she stirred it.» What does this tell you? | The juice was frozen solid | The juice had been spilled | * The juice was the same all the way through | Bits were floating in it
test: What is the opposite of homogeneous? | Hollow | * Heterogeneous | Heavy | Homonym
exam: Which sentence uses homogeneous correctly? | The lemonade was homogeneous, with sand floating in the top. | The sweets were homogeneous, with every colour and flavour mixed in. | Her homogeneous mood changed to a sunny smile. | * The town became less homogeneous after many families from different countries moved there.
